      "body": "inversed_ethane_ethylene_separation → selectivity"
    },
    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] use the alternative double-bent strategy instead of a strategy requiring both binding-angle and binding-site-distance matching → avoids the need for binding-site-distance matching in less flexible kagome lattices"
    },
    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] use a double-bent-ligand strategy by combining a bent dicarboxylate layer-forming ligand with a bent N-donor pillaring ligand → enables construction of pillar-layered structures with corrugated layers and targeted three-dimensional kagome lattices"
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparison",
      "body": "the reported material with IAST selectivity 5.1 vs activated carbon: winner=subject_a on IAST_selectivity"
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparison",
      "body": "CPM-63a vs CPM-63m: winner=tie on gas_adsorption_properties_across_test_gases"
    }
